<div class="hero" style="max-width:600px">
  <h1 style="font-size:2rem;margin-top:.75rem">Send something sensitive?<br><span class="accent">It burns after reading</span></h1>
  <p style="color:var(--dim);font-size:.9rem;margin-top:.75rem;line-height:1.7">Paste whatever you need to share &mdash; passwords, keys, credentials &mdash; and we'll give you a link that self-destructs after it's opened. AES-256-GCM encrypted, never stored in plaintext.</p>

  <form method="POST" action="/new" id="create-form" style="margin-top:2rem">
    <div class="fg">
      <textarea name="content" id="content" rows="5" class="ft" placeholder="Paste a password, API key, credentials, anything sensitive..." required maxlength="500000"></textarea>
      <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;margin-top:.3rem"><span class="fhint">AES-256-GCM encrypted</span><span class="fhint" id="char-count">0</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="fr">
      <div class="fg">
        <label class="fl" for="expiry">Expires</label>
        <select name="expiry" id="expiry" class="fs">
          <option value="1">1 hour</option>
          <option value="24" selected>24 hours</option>
          <option value="168">7 days</option>
          <option value="720">30 days</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <div class="fg">
        <label class="fl" for="max_views">Views</label>
        <select name="max_views" id="max_views" class="fs">
          <option value="1" selected>1 (burn after reading)</option>
          <option value="3">3</option>
          <option value="5">5</option>
          <option value="10">10</option>
          <option value="100">100</option>
        </select>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="fg">
      <label class="fl" for="password">Password (optional)</label>
      <input type="text" name="password" id="password" class="fi" placeholder="Adds a second factor">
    </div>

    <% if (user) { %>
    <div class="fr">
      <div class="fg">
        <label class="fl" for="label">Label (private)</label>
        <input type="text" name="label" id="label" class="fi" placeholder="e.g. staging DB creds" maxlength="255">
      </div>
      <div class="fg" style="display:flex;align-items:flex-end;padding-bottom:1.25rem">
        <label class="fcheck"><input type="checkbox" name="notify"> Notify on view</label>
      </div>
    </div>
    <% } %>

    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-lime btn-full fire-glow-hover">Encrypt &amp; create link</button>
  </form>

  <% if (!user) { %><p style="text-align:center;font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);margin-top:1.25rem"><a href="/register">Sign up</a> to track your notes and get notified when they're read.</p><% } %>
</div>

<% if (adsenseId) { %><div class="ad-slot"><ins class="adsbygoogle" style="display:block" data-ad-client="<%= adsenseId %>" data-ad-slot="auto" data-ad-format="auto" data-full-width-responsive="true"></ins><script>(adsbygoogle = window.adsbygoogle || []).push({});</script></div><% } %>

<div class="section-dark" id="how">
  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-tag">// how it works</div>
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <div class="grid-3">
      <div>
        <div style="font-family:var(--mono);color:var(--lime);font-size:.7rem;margin-bottom:.5rem">01</div>
        <h3 style="font-size:1.1rem;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:.4rem">Paste your secret</h3>
        <p style="color:var(--dim);font-size:.875rem;line-height:1.6">Whatever it is gets AES-256-GCM encrypted before anything touches a database</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div style="font-family:var(--mono);color:var(--lime);font-size:.7rem;margin-bottom:.5rem">02</div>
        <h3 style="font-size:1.1rem;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:.4rem">Send the link</h3>
        <p style="color:var(--dim);font-size:.875rem;line-height:1.6">Over Slack, email, text, wherever &mdash; the actual secret stays encrypted until the recipient opens it</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div style="font-family:var(--mono);color:var(--lime);font-size:.7rem;margin-bottom:.5rem">03</div>
        <h3 style="font-size:1.1rem;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:.4rem">It burns</h3>
        <p style="color:var(--dim);font-size:.875rem;line-height:1.6">Once read, the content is permanently deleted and the link goes dead &mdash; you can get notified when that happens</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="section">
  <div class="section-tag">// why not just use slack</div>
  <h2>Because Slack search is forever</h2>
  <p style="color:var(--dim);font-size:.9rem;margin-top:.5rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;max-width:600px;line-height:1.7">Every password pasted in a Slack channel is searchable by anyone in that workspace, indefinitely. Same with email. These tools weren't designed for secrets.</p>
  <div style="max-width:700px">
    <div class="feat">
      <div class="feat-num">01</div>
      <div><div class="feat-title">Key-separated encryption</div><div class="feat-desc">The decryption key only exists in the URL &mdash; we store a hash for lookup, never the key itself. Even if our database leaked, the ciphertext would be useless.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="feat">
      <div class="feat-num">02</div>
      <div><div class="feat-title">Configurable burn</div><div class="feat-desc">Set it to burn after 1 view, or allow up to 10,000 reads for something the whole team needs. Your call.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="feat">
      <div class="feat-num">03</div>
      <div><div class="feat-title">Viewer intel</div><div class="feat-desc">Know when your note was opened, and from what browser and OS. Burn notifications show up on your dashboard in real-time.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="feat">
      <div class="feat-num">04</div>
      <div><div class="feat-title">Password lock</div><div class="feat-desc">Share the link in one channel, the password in another. Neither is useful on its own &mdash; two-factor sharing, basically.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="feat">
      <div class="feat-num">05</div>
      <div><div class="feat-title">Operation codenames</div><div class="feat-desc">Every note gets a random codename like "Shadow Falcon" so you can track them on your dashboard without exposing what's inside.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="feat">
      <div class="feat-num">06</div>
      <div><div class="feat-title">REST API</div><div class="feat-desc">Automate it from your CI/CD pipeline with a single curl command. Full docs at <a href="/api-docs">/api-docs</a>.</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="section-dark">
  <div class="section" style="text-align:center;max-width:600px">
    <div class="section-tag">// updates</div>
    <h2>Stay in the loop</h2>
    <p style="color:var(--dim);margin-bottom:1.5rem;font-size:.85rem">We send occasional updates, no spam</p>
    <form method="POST" action="/subscribe" style="display:flex;gap:0;border:1px solid var(--border)">
      <input type="hidden" name="source" value="landing">
      <input type="email" name="email" required placeholder="you@company.com" class="fi" style="border:none;flex:1">
      <button type="submit" class="btn btn-lime" style="white-space:nowrap">Subscribe</button>
    </form>
  </div>
</div>

<% if (adsenseId) { %><div class="ad-slot"><ins class="adsbygoogle" style="display:block" data-ad-client="<%= adsenseId %>" data-ad-slot="auto" data-ad-format="auto" data-full-width-responsive="true"></ins><script>(adsbygoogle = window.adsbygoogle || []).push({});</script></div><% } %>
